1?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rayamazaky","html_url":"https://github.com/rayamazaky","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rayamazaky/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rayamazaky/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rayamazaky/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rayamazaky/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rayamazaky/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rayamazaky/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rayamazaky/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rayamazaky/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rayamazaky/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-12T18:11:29Z","updated_at":"2026-04-12T18:11:29Z","body":"Hi! Yes, AI was used to help identify and fix these bugs. I ran an automated analysis across the `core/` and `servers/` directories to find common bug patterns (null pointer dereferences, race conditions, division by zero, integer overflows, etc.), then verified each finding manually against the source code before filing separate issues and creating individual PRs for each fix.\n\nEach PR is a single focused change that builds successfully. Happy to adjust any of the fixes based on review feedback.\n\nRegarding the purpose — we created these issues to help with bug funding/awareness. Each issue documents a verified source-level bug with code references so maintainers can prioritize them regardless of whether these specific PR fixes are accepted as-is.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4232254504/reactions","total_count":6,"+1":0,"-1":1,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":5,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/go